{"parentUuid":"25cee0ee-53c7-4b33-8c7e-022f6a6af0ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg5o2snw6NoqeuCNEBx7D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The video files and recordings are removed from the repo, and the code is pushed to GitHub without the video. `main` is now at `996fd4e`.\n\n**What's left of the video:**\n- **Final film:** `~/Desktop/mochi-final-video/mochi-product-film.mp4`, outside the repo. I also moved the captions file `mochi-product-film.srt` there.\n- **GitHub:** it has no video at all. No `.mp4` or `.mov` file is tracked.\n\n**What I removed:**\n- The whole `video/` folder (the HyperFrames projects, stills, audio and renders, about 520 MB).\n- All 7 screen recordings from the repo folder.\n- `docs/demo/` and the older `mochi-demo-mobile.mp4`, which had been pushed earlier. It's gone from the latest commit but remains in git history.\n- The README and post-draft lines that pointed at the videos.\n\n**What I kept:**\n- **Product photos:** the `Product Images` folder and your original `Mochi Teal Ribbon Logo.png` are still there. They're your own files, and the logo is also in `docs/brand/`. Both are ignored by git so they won't be pushed. Say if you want them deleted too.\n- **App video feature:** I did not touch `backend/app/services/video/`, because that is Mochi's real video-ad feature and not video production.\n- **Screenshots:** the screenshots in `docs/images/` are still in.\n\nNothing else is pending locally."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_read_input_tokens":773109,"output_tokens":485,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_token